  "worked_solution": "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2a-\\frac{5}{4}b=30 & |\\times 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}a+b=-6 & |\\times 5\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}8a-5b=120 \\\\ a+5b=-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $b$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8a-\\cancel{5b} & =120 \\\\ a+\\cancel{5b} & =-30 \\\\ (8a+a) & =(120-30) \\\\ 9a & =90 \\\\ a & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $a=10$ into the second equation to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+5b & =-30 \\\\ 10+5b & =-30 \\\\ 5b & =-40 \\\\ b & =-\\frac{40}{5} \\\\ b & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $a=10,\\,b=-8.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
